<title>USA: US budget deal unlikely by early next week - Daschle.</title>
<headline>US budget deal unlikely by early next week - Daschle.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Democratic Senate Minority Leader Tom Daschle said on Thursday he thought it was unlikely there would be a U.S. balanced budget deal by early next week.</p>
<p>Asked after a meeting with President Bill Clinton about speculation that a deal might be struck early next week, Daschle told reporters: &quot;I would say today that's unlikely.&quot;</p>
<p>He also said that large tax cuts tended to undermine efforts to protect Democratic priorities.</p>
</text>
